{%- liquid
  assign is_home = false
  if template.name == 'index'
    assign is_home = true
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  On a made-to-order product page the site-wide "Cash on delivery nationwide"
  strapline sits directly above the buy box, which asks for a 50% deposit.
  Swap the middle claim on those pages so the top of the page and the buy box
  agree. Everywhere else is untouched — plain COD remains true for the rest of
  the catalogue.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign announce_mto = false
  if template.name == 'product'
    if product.metafields.custom.made_to_order.value == true or product.type contains 'Jacket'
      assign announce_mto = true
    endif
  endif
-%}
<div class="kv-announce" id="kv-announce">
  Free delivery over <b>PKR 5,500</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; {% if announce_mto %}Made to order · book with 50%{% else %}Cash on delivery nationwide{% endif %} &nbsp;·&nbsp; 100% genuine leather
</div>

